-- title:
--   The chosen uniformiser at a place has order one
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $N \ge 1$ a natural number, and let $F = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,N$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the two series $\mathrm{jqModC}\,K = q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNum}$ (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$, with its integral coefficients pushed into $K$) and $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,K\,N$, the image of that series under the substitution $q \mapsto q^{N}$. Let $x$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, that is: a valuation subring of $F$ that contains $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,F(a)$ for every $a \in K$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring. For $f \in F$ write $x.\mathrm{ord}\,f = -\log$ of the value of $f$ under the $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation attached to the height-one prime of the valuation subring of $x$. The element $\mathrm{unif}\,N\,K\,x \in F$ is by definition a Hilbert-$\varepsilon$ choice of an element $\pi$ satisfying $x.\mathrm{ord}\,\pi = 1$. The assertion is that this chosen element does satisfy $x.\mathrm{ord}(\mathrm{unif}\,N\,K\,x) = 1$, i.e. the defining predicate of the choice is satisfiable.
--
--   This is the basic fact that a place of a function field admits a uniformiser, specialised to the function field of the modular curve of level $N$ over $K$ and to the globally fixed choice of uniformiser at each place. It is the only property of that choice used downstream, where the uniformiser serves as local coordinate for the leading-coefficient and residue constructions in the supersingular Hecke-module computations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ord_unif.lean

